From 4a88e67f96e55ab354e94d65d8dd5b98d5171252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:56:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: head for the nearest free staircase when desperate

The 'Desperation Head for stairs' check in borg_caution() measures how
far the nearest free up and down staircases are, then dashes for one
that is a step or two away.  Both scans kept the farthest staircase
instead ('skip the closer ones'), so a second, distant staircase of the
same kind on the level hid a staircase right next to the borg.

A badly hurt borg with a monster beside it and an up staircase two steps
away therefore skipped the dash whenever it also knew a far staircase,
and fell through to its other escapes; with no teleport available it
read Word of Recall and stayed next to the monster.

Keep the nearest free staircase in both scans, matching their comments
and the closeness tests that follow.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#153.

(cherry picked from commit 62768100602b693ed5845f0e5749830563d7e3b3)
---
 src/borg/borg-caution.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-caution.c b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
index 7cc354e76..19cdf5c0d 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-caution.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
@@ -1306,8 +1306,8 @@ bool borg_caution(void)
             if (ag->kill)
                 continue;
 
-            /* skip the closer ones */
-            if (b_j >= j)
+            /* skip the farther ones */
+            if (b_j <= j && b_j != -1)
                 continue;
 
             /* track it */
@@ -1321,15 +1321,15 @@ bool borg_caution(void)
 
             ag = &borg_grids[y][x];
 
-            /* How far is the nearest up stairs */
+            /* How far is the nearest down stairs */
             m = distance(borg.c, loc(x, y));
 
             /* Skip stairs if a monster is on the stair */
             if (ag->kill)
                 continue;
 
-            /* skip the closer ones */
-            if (b_m >= m)
+            /* skip the farther ones */
+            if (b_m <= m && b_m != -1)
                 continue;
 
             /* track it */
